491
00:24:33,540 --> 00:24:40,720
wildcard break is, um, in the, in the, uh, definition, uh, you know, where it is at,

492
00:24:40,720 --> 00:24:42,780
uh, in the subdomain structure, that sort of thing.

493
00:24:43,140 --> 00:24:46,680
And then you're also resolving it multiple times with multiple resolvers to try to get,

494
00:24:47,100 --> 00:24:52,500
um, an idea of what IPs are being round Robin returned in that, in that, and then creating

495
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:56,400
a profile of sorts, uh, for what that wildcard should look like.

496
00:24:56,400 --> 00:25:01,980
And then when you resolve things, which match that wildcard, um, in the subdomain level,

497
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:06,000
but do not match that response, then, you know, you've got a diamond in the rough, something

498
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:09,840
that most people, other people won't find because they're just going to be saying, all right,

