1351
01:08:31,940 --> 01:08:33,900
So the term is JS wasting.

1352
01:08:33,900 --> 01:08:38,360
And it's essentially the concept that functions in JS

1353
01:08:38,360 --> 01:08:41,360
defined using and some other objects as well,

1354
01:08:41,360 --> 01:08:43,840
but mostly for this case functions,

1355
01:08:43,840 --> 01:08:47,380
defined using the function keyword,

1356
01:08:47,380 --> 01:08:49,340
despite where they are in the flow,

1357
01:08:49,340 --> 01:08:53,760
will be hoisted to the top of the script execution flow.

1358
01:08:53,760 --> 01:08:56,240
So if you define a function at the very bottom

1359
01:08:56,240 --> 01:08:58,980
using the function keyword of a script tag,

1360
01:08:58,980 --> 01:09:00,740
and you call that function above where

1361
01:09:00,740 --> 01:09:02,560
that function is defined, it'll work.

1362
01:09:02,560 --> 01:09:05,000
Because the function definition is getting moved up

1363
01:09:05,000 --> 01:09:09,140
to the top of the script.

1364
01:09:09,140 --> 01:09:11,640
So in this scenario, what we were able to do

1365
01:09:11,640 --> 01:09:14,960
was define the function x.

1366
01:09:14,960 --> 01:09:19,400
And what that would do is it would hoist the definition

1367
01:09:19,400 --> 01:09:20,000
up to the top.

1368
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:22,740
And now the variable x now contains a valid function.

1369
01:09:22,740 --> 01:09:23,740
OK?

1370
01:09:23,740 --> 01:09:27,440
So when you try to access the property y on x,

1371
01:09:27,440 --> 01:09:30,640
you don't get an error, but you get y is undefined.

1372
01:09:30,640 --> 01:09:36,380
Then it will attempt to call the undefined y because of the function

1373
01:09:36,380 --> 01:09:37,320
call.

1374
01:09:37,320 --> 01:09:40,380
And when it does that, it will parse the parameters that

1375
01:09:40,380 --> 01:09:42,240
are being passed into that function.

1376
01:09:42,240 --> 01:09:44,400
And at that point, when it parses the parameters,

1377
01:09:44,400 --> 01:09:47,960
you can do a function call in the parameters themselves.

1378
01:09:47,960 --> 01:09:51,120
And that will get executed before it attempts to call y,

1379
01:09:51,120 --> 01:09:55,140
which will inevitably fail because you can't call undefined.

1380
01:09:55,140 --> 01:09:58,900
And in that way, we were able to get arbitrary script execution

1381
01:09:58,900 --> 01:10:02,140
and pop it into an XSS because of this concept called JS wasting.

